# Architecture

Three processes over one PostgreSQL database, with domain logic in packages that
none of them own.

- `apps/api` — Fastify. Auth, authorization, validation, audit, transactions.
- `apps/web` — Next.js. Renders. Holds no business rules.
- `apps/worker` — scheduled jobs. Single instance.
- `packages/core`, `packages/permissions` — pure domain logic, no I/O.

## Rules

Domain logic goes in `packages/core` as a pure function with unit tests, even
when only one endpoint uses it. That is what keeps the rules testable without a
database.

The web app never re-implements a rule the API enforces. Even the sidebar comes
from `/api/v1/me/navigation`, built by the same permission checks — so the menu
and the authorization rules cannot drift apart.

Do not add a dependency for something you could write in thirty lines. The S3
driver implements SigV4 directly rather than carrying the AWS SDK.

Do not rewrite working architecture because you prefer a different framework.

Read `docs/architecture.md` before making a structural change.
